  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Title">Assistant: how requests are read</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Hint">The assistant always finds mods in the Steam Workshop itself and checks them the same way. Here you only choose what reads your request: a simple word list or a neural network that understands any wording.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Words">Built-in word list</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Words.Hint">Works at once, no neural network. Knows themes ("fantasy", "space"…), "for a weak PC", "stable", "no magic", "20 mods", names of games and films.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model">RimForge's neural network on this PC</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Hint">Understands any request ("I want to play a cannibal tribe in the desert"). Free, no sign-up, the request never leaves your PC. One download of ≈ 2.4 GB; 8 GB of memory or more is best. A graphics card speeds it up but isn't needed.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Download">Download ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Brain.Model.Download">Download the Qwen3 4B model (Apache 2.0 licence) and llama.cpp to run it (MIT). You can stop the download and continue later.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Pause">Pause</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Brain.Model.Pause">Stop the download; it continues from the same place later.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Delete">Delete</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Brain.Model.Delete">Delete the neural network from disk. The assistant goes back to the word list.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.NotInstalled">Not downloaded.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Downloading">Downloading… {0}%</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Installed">Downloaded · {0} on disk. Starts by itself when needed and stops after 10 idle minutes.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Ready">The neural network is downloaded — the assistant now understands any request.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Paused">The download stopped — press "Download" to continue.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Failed">Failed: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.DeleteTitle">Delete the assistant's neural network?</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.DeleteText">This frees {0}. The assistant will read requests with the word list; you can download the network again at any time.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Model.Name">RimForge's network</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server">Another neural network</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Hint">A program on this PC (Ollama, LM Studio) or a service with a key (OpenRouter, Groq, Google Gemini, DeepSeek, Mistral, OpenAI). The request goes where you point it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Where">Where</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Url">Address</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Key">Key</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.GetKey">Get a key</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Brain.Server.GetKey">Open the service's page that gives out keys. Many services have a free tier.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Model">Model</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Check">Check and turn on</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Brain.Server.Check">Ask for the list of models, pick a fitting one, make sure it answers and use it for the assistant.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Checking">Checking…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Ok">Works: {0}. The assistant now reads requests with this network.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Failed">No answer: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Timeout">timed out</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.NoModels">The server answered but has no models. In Ollama, install one with "ollama pull qwen3:4b".</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.PickModel">Pick a model in the list and press "Check" again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Server.Found">Found on this PC: {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Preset.Custom">Custom address</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Using">Reads requests: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.UsingWords">Reads requests: word list</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Brain.Open">How the assistant reads requests — word list or neural network. Open the settings.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Thinking">Reading the request…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Starting">Starting the neural network… (the first start can take up to a minute)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.BadAnswer">unclear answer</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Brain.Fallback">The neural network didn't help ({0}) — read the request with the word list.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.Tab.Translations">Translations</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.Tab.TranslationsCount">Translations · {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Ws.TabTranslations">Find Workshop translations for the modpack's mods that lack your language.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Hint">RimForge checks the current modpack: which mods have no translation into the chosen language (or less than 70% of it), and finds translations for them in the Steam Workshop — single ones and big packs. Tick what you want and press "Download and turn on": translations go into the modpack right after their mods.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Language">Language:</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Trn.Language">Which language to find translations for. By default the game's language (or RimForge's, if the game is in English).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Find">Find translations</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Trn.Find">Check the modpack's mods and search the Workshop for translations.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.PickLanguage">Pick the language to find translations for.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Checking">Checking which mods are not translated…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Searching">Searching the Workshop: {0} of {1}…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.SomeFailed">Some searches failed (Steam connection) — try again later.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Failed">Could not find translations: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Summary">The modpack has {0} mods: translated into "{4}" — {1}, not translated — {2}, without text (nothing to translate) — {3}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.NothingFound">No new translations found. Either everything is translated, or the Workshop has no translations for these mods yet.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.GameNote">The game itself is set to "{0}". Translations into "{1}" work once you choose it in RimWorld: Options → Language.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Untranslated">Not translated into "{1}": {0} — find translations</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Trn.Light">These mods of the modpack have no translation. RimForge will search the Workshop for translations.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.For">for: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.ForPack">for {1} mods: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Pack">pack: {0} mods</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Badge.Installed">downloaded</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Badge.Old">older game version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Trn.Old">The translation isn't marked for your game version — some texts may not match. That's why it is unticked.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Badge.Fresher">fresher translation</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Replaces">replaces the outdated "{0}"</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.NotFound">No translation found ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Trn.NotFound">The Workshop has no translations for these mods (or the mod is not from the Workshop).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Apply">Download and turn on ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Trn.Apply">Download the ticked translations from the Steam Workshop and turn them on in the current modpack after their mods.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.ApplyHint">Downloaded translations turn on at once, the others when they arrive.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.Done">Translations are on. Mods translated: {0}, {1} translated on average.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.DoneWeak">Not fully translated: {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.NewMods">New mods without a translation into "{1}": {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Trn.FindShort">Find translations</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Asst.Topic.translations">Translations</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Asst.Translations">I also found translations into "{1}" for the pack's mods ({0}) — they are in the "Translations" group on the right.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Title">Game folders</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Hint">RimForge finds them by itself. If the game or the mods are somewhere else, choose the folder by hand; "Auto" goes back to the one found automatically.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.CopyNote">A copy of the game from the library is chosen — it has its own folders. These paths belong to the installed game.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.game">Game</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.game.Hint">The folder with RimWorldWin64.exe.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.workshop">Workshop mods</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.workshop.Hint">Where Steam downloads subscriptions: …\steamapps\workshop\content\294100.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.local">Local mods</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.local.Hint">The Mods folder inside the game — the only place the game takes non-Steam mods from.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.config">Settings and saves</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.config.Hint">The game's mod list, settings and saves. If it is not the usual folder, RimForge passes it to the game at launch.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.library">RimForge library</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.library.Hint">Copies of the game and frozen mods.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.NotFound">not found</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Status.Auto">found automatically</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Status.Custom">chosen by hand</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Status.Missing">not found — choose it</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Choose">Choose…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Auto">Auto</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Changed">{0}: now {1}. The mod list was read again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Reset">{0}: found automatically again ({1}).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Wrong.game">There is no RimWorld in "{0}". Choose the folder with RimWorldWin64.exe (and the Data folder).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Wrong.workshop">There are no Workshop mods in "{0}". Usually it is …\steamapps\workshop\content\294100.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Paths.Wrong.config">There are no RimWorld settings in "{0}" (no Config or Saves folder). Usually it is …\AppData\LocalLow\Ludeon Studios\RimWorld by Ludeon Studios.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Paths.Choose">Choose the folder by hand</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Paths.Reset">Forget your folder and find it automatically again</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Paths.Open">Open the folder in Explorer</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Splitter">Drag to make the panels wider or narrower. Double-click to put them back.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Row.Downloading">Downloading from the Workshop</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Dl.Footer">Open downloads</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Dl.Footer.Running">Downloading mods: {0} · {1}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Dl.Footer.Starting">Downloading mods: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Dl.Footer.Waiting">Downloads are waiting ({0}) — open to see why</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.Prev">Back</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.Next">Next</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.Page">Page</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.PageOf">of {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.Go">Go</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Ws.Prev">Previous page</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Ws.Next">Next page</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Ws.PageInput">Type a page number and press Enter</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.PageFiltered">Every mod on this page is hidden by the filters (translations, old versions, abandoned). Turn the page or loosen the filters.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.PageEmpty">Steam gives nothing more on this page — go back to an earlier one.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.LastPage">Steam gives no mods beyond this — the last page is open: {0}.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.FindingLast">Page {0} is empty — Steam gives fewer pages than it promises. Looking for the last one…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Diag.Data.Texture">Same textures ({0}) in different mods — "{1}"'s are shown</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Diag.Data.Texture.Hint">{0} ship pictures under the same paths. The game shows the pictures of the mod lower in the list, "{1}". If you expect another mod's pictures, move it lower.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Diag.Data.TextureIntended">"{1}" replaces textures ({0}) — as intended</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Diag.Data.TextureIntended.Hint">{0}: pictures with the same paths. "{1}" is a retexture or an add-on to these mods, so its pictures should win. It is lower in the list — all is well.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Diag.Data.TextureMore">…and {0} more</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Diag.Why.Textures">its pictures are covered</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Group.Graphics">Retextures</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Group.Tweak">Code tweaks</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Title">Game startup</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Tip">About how long the game will take to start with this list: {0}. Click to see what each mod costs.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Source.Guess">This is an estimate from what the mods contain (textures, defs, patches, code). It gets exact after a measurement — see below.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Source.Last">The last startup took {0} (measured by Loading Progress). The mods' shares are worked out from their content.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Source.PerMod">Every mod's time was measured at the last startup (Loading Progress).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Source.PerModNew">The mods' times were measured at the last startup (Loading Progress); new mods: {0} — estimated.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Base">The game and DLC: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Mods">Mods — what they add to the startup</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Sec">s</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Row.Measured">Measured at the last startup</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Row.Guessed">Estimated from the mod's content</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Act.Get">Get Loading Progress</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Act.Get.Hint">Exact figures need the Loading Progress mod: it times every mod while the game starts. RimForge will download and enable it.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Act.Enable">Enable Loading Progress</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Act.Enable.Hint">Loading Progress is installed but not in this modpack — without it the startup isn't measured.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Act.Track">Turn on per-mod timing</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Act.Track.Hint">Loading Progress only times the whole startup. RimForge will turn on its per-mod timing and its report in its settings.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Act.WaitLaunch">Timing is on — start the game once and every mod's exact time will be here.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.Enabled">Loading Progress is on in the modpack.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.TrackingOn">Per-mod timing is on. After the next game start every mod's exact time will be here.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Lt.GameRunning">Close the game first: it rewrites the mods' settings when it exits.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Title">RimForge {0} is out</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Text">You have {0}; {1} is available. Download and install it? It takes a minute; modpacks and settings stay as they are.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Notes">What's new:</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Install">Download and install</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Skip">Skip this version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Downloading">Downloading the RimForge update: {0}%</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.ReadyTitle">RimForge {0} is downloaded</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.ReadyText">The file checks out. Restart RimForge now? Unsaved list changes will be saved. If later, the update goes in when you close RimForge.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Restart">Restart now</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Later">Later</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.AtExit">The update will go in when you close RimForge.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.NotInstalled">The update is downloaded: {0}. This copy of RimForge isn't the usual RimForge.exe, so replace the file by hand.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Upd.Failed">Couldn't update RimForge: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Ws.Tab.Collections">Collections</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Ws.TabCollections">Players' ready modpacks from the Steam Workshop: open one, look through its mods and pictures, make it your own modpack.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Coll.SearchHint">Words in the collection's name, e.g. medieval, vanilla expanded, realistic</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Coll.Search">Search collections by words. Press Enter.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Coll.Sort">How to order the collections</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Coll.Size">How many mods a collection holds</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollSort.Week">Popular this week</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollSort.AllTime">Popular of all time</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollSort.Newest">Newest</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollSort.Updated">Recently updated</sys:String>
