  <sys:String x:Key="Badge.Collection">COLLECTION</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Coll.OpenHint">click to open</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.Mods">mods: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.Favorites">favourited by {0} · {1} views</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.ModsTitle">Mods in the collection</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.About">About the collection</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.Loading">Reading the collection's mods…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.Summary">{0} in all: {1} already here, {2} to download ({3}).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.RemovedCount">Removed from the Workshop: {0} — they won't be included.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.Have">already here</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.Removed">removed from the Workshop</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.Create">Create modpack ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="CollC.CreateDownload">Create modpack and download ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.CollC.Create">A new, separate modpack of the ticked mods. Missing ones are downloaded and take their places; the current modpack stays as it is.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.CollC.Row">Show or hide the mod's description</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Gallery.Open">Open full screen</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Gallery.Prev">Previous picture</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.Gallery.Next">Next picture</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Gallery.WatchVideo">Watch the video</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Gallery.Keys">← → or the wheel to browse · Esc to close</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Msg.GameVersionChanged">The game changed version: it was {0}, now it is {1}. I re-read the mods and checked the list for the new version — have a look and press Play again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Open">Download another version…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.GameDl.Open">Download an old (1.0–1.5) or the test version of RimWorld straight into the RimForge library. The Steam game stays as it is.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Title">Download a RimWorld version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Hint">The version is downloaded with Valve's official tool (SteamCMD) into a folder of the library and shows up in the list of games as a copy, with its own saves and mods. The game Steam installed doesn't change.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.GameDl.Hide">Hide the window (the download goes on)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Installing">Getting SteamCMD ready for the first time — Valve's official tool for downloading games (about 150 MB, only once)…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Reading">Reading the RimWorld versions from Steam…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.NoBranches">Steam returned no versions.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.SetupFailed">Couldn't get the download ready: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Retry">Try again</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Current">Current version (as in Steam)</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Testing">Test version</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.TestingBadge">NEW · IN TESTING</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Updated">updated {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Account">Steam account:</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.AccountHint">the login you use for Steam</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Tip.GameDl.Account">The login of the Steam account that owns RimWorld. RimForge never asks for or keeps the password — you type it only in SteamCMD's window.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Start">Download</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.LoginText">Sign in to Steam through SteamCMD once, as “{0}”.&#x0a;&#x0a;Press “Sign in to Steam” — SteamCMD's black window opens. Type your password there and, if asked, the Steam Guard code (or approve the sign-in in the Steam app). RimForge doesn't see the password. When the window closes by itself, the download starts.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.LoginWaiting">Waiting for you to sign in as “{0}” in SteamCMD's window…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.LoginFailed">The sign-in as “{0}” wasn't saved. Check the login and try again.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.SignIn">Sign in to Steam</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Back">Back</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Starting">Starting to download {0}…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Progress">Downloading {0}: {1} of ≈{2}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.ProgressNoTotal">Downloading {0}: {1}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.CanHide">You can close this window — the download goes on, its progress shows on the game version button.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Finishing">Downloaded. Putting the game into the library…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Failed">The download failed: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.NotOwned">Steam says this account doesn't own RimWorld (or this version).</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Cancelled">Version download cancelled, the downloaded files were removed.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.ModsTitle">RimWorld {0} downloaded — which mods to take?</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.ModsText">The modpack “{0}” has {1} mods. For version {2}, {3} fit and {4} don't.&#x0a;&#x0a;Take the fitting mods into this version of the game? They are stored in the library as they are now and won't be updated.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.ModsMisfit">Don't fit: {0}</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.ModsTake">Take the fitting ones ({0})</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.ModsNone">No mods</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Linking">Putting the mods into the new version of the game…</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.DoneTitle">RimWorld {0} is ready</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.DoneText">RimWorld {0} is in the RimForge library, with its own saves and mods.&#x0a;&#x0a;Switch to it now? You can switch any time with the game version button at the top of the window.</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="GameDl.Later">Later</sys:String>
  <sys:String x:Key="Game.DownloadedDetails">Downloaded from Steam ({0}) {1} · mods: {2}</sys:String>
</ResourceDictionary>
